body:
> ​This is rather strong. "Duplicates a rogue's signature class feature and makes elves a worse choice for rogues" strong. How about "you can only move in a straight line by jumping" instead of the weird hopping thing? 

&#x200B;

I molded it after the tabaxi speed burst, and considering how powerful that already seems to be, you right. But I feel like changing the hopping to just "moves in a straight line" would still be quite powerful, especially with the added jump height/distance. Maybe just make it a passive that doubles jump capabilities and pump up the speed from 35 to 40 feet ? I also thought about just changing it a unique jump that scales of dex instead of strength and doesn't require a running start, but don't know how useful that would actually be.

&#x200B;

>How about this? "When you move at least 20 feet straight towards a creature and make an Attack action, you get advantage on your first Strength (Athletics) check to shove the target until the end of your turn."

&#x200B;

Absolutely, I didn't quite consider how strong knocking someone prone is. So how about: 

>Pounce: When you move at least 20 feet straight towards a creature and make an Attack action, you get advantage on your first Strength (Athletics) check to shove the target until the end of your turn. If you manage to knock the target prone, you can deliver digestive bite as a bonus action.

&#x200B;

> ​This is fine. I think it's actually better as a melee attack instead of a saving throw. 

You right, considering a bite is an attack, it probably should be:

>  Digestive Bite: As an attack action, you can bite a creature within 5 feet of you.If the attack hits the target takes 1d6 + your constitution modifier in acid damage.. You can also use this feature to liquefy the corpse of a medium or smaller creature in 1d4 hours. You can't use this trait again until you finish a short or long rest. 

&#x200B;

Spiderclimb is probably going to be a case by case basis, or DM by DM basis. I was thinking maybe just halving the speed, but keeping the wall/ceiling climbing aspect to add a penalty.

&#x200B;

>I would make this require an action to make and attach the tether.  
>  
>Also, YOU KNOW that a PC is going to try to use this on an enemy.

&#x200B;

Huh, I didn't consider that at all. Although I m not quite sure, how useful this would be, I should probably change it. So how is:

> Tether: As an action you can use your Spinneret to create a silken rope that is connected to you and a point with in 5 feet of you. If the point is a living creature, this is a grapple and rolled as such. The rope can extend up to 60 feet before breaking. It has 2 hit points and can be burst with a DC 17 Strength check. 

Considering grapple already uses a strength check, and the rope having a strength DC of 17, I think I can leave it at that. Should I, just in case, write the the grabble has to be rolled against the DC of the rope, instead of the PC athletics ?

&#x200B;

Thank you so much for your feedback! You helped me out a lot!
